## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical lazy-loading with ES module dynamic import, closures, and promises in a dashboard scenario.

## Key Concepts
- dynamic import() and module caching
- per-widget state gated by closures
- IntersectionObserver for visibility-triggered loads
- cancellation with AbortController
- timeout handling and graceful fallbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
function createWidgetLoader(){
  const registry = new Map();
  function loadWidget(id){
    const entry = registry.get(id);
    if (entry && entry.state === 'ready') return Promise.resolve(entry.module);
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const p = import(`./widgets/${id}.js`).then(m => {
      if (ctrl.signal.aborted) throw new Error('aborted');
      registry.set(id, { state: 'ready', module: m, promise: Promise.resolve(m) });
      return m;
    }).catch(e => { registry.set(id, { state: 'error' }); throw e; });
    registry.set(id, { state: 'loading', promise: p, controller: ctrl });
    return p;
  }
  return { loadWidget, isLoaded: id => registry.get(id)?.state === 'ready' };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about Lighthouse metrics, bundle sizing, and lazy-loading in a real-world SPA.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic code splitting and route-level bundles
- IntersectionObserver-driven lazy loading
- Lighthouse-like budgets and CI automation
- Progressive image loading and origin preconnect

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, { useState, useEffect, lazy, Suspense } from 'react'

const HeavyChart = lazy(() => import('./HeavyChart'))

export default function Dashboard(){
  const [showChart, setShowChart] = useState(false)
  const ref = React.useRef(null)
  useEffect(() => {
    const obs = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) { setShowChart(true); obs.disconnect() }
    }, { rootMargin: '200px' })
    if (ref.current) obs.observe(ref.current)
    return () => obs.disconnect()
  }, [])
  return (
    <div ref={ref}>
      {showChart ? (
        <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading chart…</div>}>
          <HeavyChart />
        </Suspense>
      ) : (
        <div>Chart placeholder</div>
      )}
    </div>
  )
}
```

